preguntas.respuestaEn:
"Serverless does not mean there are no servers; it means I do not manage them. I write a function, upload it, and the provider runs it only when a request arrives, scales it automatically and charges per execution. For example, on Vercel, Netlify or AWS Lambda I can create a function that receives a contact form and sends an email, without building a full backend. The downside is the cold start: the first call after a while without traffic can take a bit longer."

```js
// AWS Lambda: solo se ejecuta cuando llega una petición
export const handler = async (event) => {
  const datos = JSON.parse(event.body);
  return { statusCode: 200, body: JSON.stringify({ recibido: datos.email }) };
};
```
